Teach the Makefile's OS-detection ladder about NetBSD.

Upstream cloudflared builds on freebsd and openbsd but has never carried a
netbsd branch, so `go env GOOS` on NetBSD falls straight through to the
$(error) at the end of the ladder and `gmake cloudflared` dies before it ever
invokes the compiler. Everything else in upstream's Makefile works unmodified
on all three BSDs, which is why this is the fork's only Makefile deviation.

This replaced a full-file Makefile overlay frozen at a 2024-era upstream base.
That copy silently overrode every upstream Makefile change; when upstream
de-vendored in 2026.9.0 the frozen copy kept `-mod=vendor` and all five BSD
legs failed with `go: inconsistent vendoring`.

If upstream ever adds netbsd itself, the `git apply --reverse --check` in
.github/workflows/update-cloudflared.yml will detect it and tell you to delete
this file.

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -97,6 +97,10 @@ else ifeq ($(LOCAL_OS),windows)
     TARGET_OS ?= windows
 else ifeq ($(LOCAL_OS),freebsd)
     TARGET_OS ?= freebsd
+# BSD fork delta: upstream ships freebsd and openbsd but not netbsd, so
+# without this branch `go env GOOS` on NetBSD hits the $(error) below.
+else ifeq ($(LOCAL_OS),netbsd)
+    TARGET_OS ?= netbsd
 else ifeq ($(LOCAL_OS),openbsd)
     TARGET_OS ?= openbsd
 else
